	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/audio_settings/help_strings">
		<string text="The sound and its devices, 3D audio, the volumes and voice chat."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Where the game's sound and the other players' voices play."/>
		<string text="Where the sounds around you come from. Auto and Headphones place each ahead, behind, above or below you, as the Xbox's 3D audio did on speakers and headphones alike; Speakers pans them left and right."/>
		<string text="Echoes sounds as the place you are in would, and muffles those behind walls, as the Xbox did. It costs a little of the processor."/>
		<string text="How sounds are converted to your speakers' rate. Xbox sounds as the Xbox did; Clean is clearer; Classic is brighter but harsher. Xbox and Classic cost a little less."/>
		<string text="Turns all sound off or on, at once."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="The volume of everything the game plays. 10 is the Xbox's level; up to 20 is louder."/>
		<string text="The music's volume."/>
		<string text="Every other sound: weapons, vehicles, the world and the characters' speech."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Talking to the other players in network games, your microphone and their voices' volume."/>
		<string text="A short beep each time you damage another player, as the host dealt it. A host may forbid them in its games.|The beep is a placeholder for now."/>
		<string text="In the games you host, whether the players may hear their hit sounds. A Legacy game's players cannot be told."/>
	</strings>
